{
	"info": {
		"name": "Many Faced God API v1",
		"description": "Read-only public API for MFG NPC data.\n\nContract source of truth: `openapi/v1.yaml` in the repo, served live at `{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/openapi.yaml`.\n\n## How to run\n\n1. Import the `many-faced-god.postman_environment.json` environment and select it.\n2. Set `baseUrl` if your instance is not on `http://localhost:8765`.\n3. Run the whole collection with the Collection Runner (or `newman run`).\n\nRequests run **in order** and are stateful: the `Discovery` folder probes the service, then `NPCs > List NPCs` captures a real `npcId` and `folderId` into collection variables that every later request depends on. Running a single request in the middle without seeding first may fail on an empty variable.\n\n## What the assertions cover\n\nBeyond simple 200s, these tests encode the design decisions that are easy to regress:\n\n- `challengeRating` is always an **object**, and a missing CR yields `{value:null,xp:null}` \u2014 **never `0`**.\n- Payloads are **deterministic** \u2014 two consecutive fetches of the same NPC are byte-identical (guards against `rollHitPoints()` leaking into the API).\n- `ETag` is present and `If-None-Match` returns **304**.\n- Templates never appear in `/npcs`.\n- `pageSize` is **clamped**, not rejected; bad `sort` **is** rejected.\n- CR sorts numerically (`1/8 < 1/2 < 2 < 10`), not lexically.\n- All JSON keys are camelCase.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "npcId",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "templateId",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "folderId",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "npcEtag",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "npcBody",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "test",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"// Applies to every request in the collection.",
					"pm.test('Responds within 2s', function () {",
					"    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(2000);",
					"});",
					"",
					"// Every JSON response must advertise the API version.",
					"if (pm.response.code !== 304) {",
					"    pm.test('X-MFG-API-Version header is present', function () {",
					"        pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-MFG-API-Version')).to.eql('1');",
					"    });",
					"}"
				]
			}
		}
	],
